# Adapted from the ::guru ebuild (amd64), which vendors its frontend
# node_modules as a single prebuilt, x86_64-only tarball. That tarball's
# @rollup/rollup-linux-*, @esbuild/*, and @tauri-apps/cli-linux-* optional
# native npm packages are x86_64-gnu builds only, so `npm run build` fails
# on arm64 with "Cannot find module @rollup/rollup-linux-arm64-gnu". This
# arm64-only ebuild instead fetches the exact linux/arm64/glibc npm
# dependency closure individually from registry.npmjs.org and assembles
# node_modules from those distfiles in src_prepare, so no network access
# is needed during src_compile and no prebuilt vendor blob needs to be
# hosted for arm64.
#
# The dependency closure below is locked from
# files/restic-browser-0.3.3-vaadin-23.3.25-package-lock.json.gz
# (gzipped to stay under pkgcheck's files/ size thresholds), NOT
# upstream's own package-lock.json: it pins the 24 @vaadin/* packages
# that upstream's unpinned "^23.3" range would otherwise resolve to a
# commercially licensed release (see the RESTIC_BROWSER_NPM_SRC_URI and
# LICENSE comments below). That same committed file is installed
# (decompressed) over the stock package-lock.json in src_prepare, so the
# prepared source tree, this ebuild's arrays, and the file used to
# regenerate them are always one consistent lockfile, not three copies
# that could drift apart.
#
# Regenerate the dependency arrays below with:
#   scripts/generate-restic-browser-npm-deps.py 0.3.3 \
#     app-backup/restic-browser/files/restic-browser-0.3.3-vaadin-23.3.25-package-lock.json.gz out.gen
# The generator itself refuses to emit an entry for any package whose
# lockfile-recorded license is a URL (the pattern proprietary licenses
# use, including Vaadin's), so pointing it at a fresh, unpinned lockfile
# fails loudly instead of producing a mislicensed ebuild.

